= The Treaty Is Signed

Scheidemann would not sign, and on 20 June his cabinet resigned. Gustav Bauer, a trade union man, formed a government of the Social Democrats and the Centre; the Democrats walked out rather than share the blame. On 28 June, in the Hall of Mirrors, two ministers nobody had heard of signed the treaty.

The Freikorps officers who crushed Berlin and Munich for the Republic now say the Republic has betrayed them. Some of them talk openly of a dictatorship.
